//! T-PG.6.4: every statement pgbench sends parses to PostgreSQL 19's tree, byte for byte as the
//! oracle prints it (`nodeToStringWithLocations`). The statements are pgbench.c's at the vendored
//! commit: TPC-B's with its variables substituted as `-M simple` substitutes them (a negative and a
//! positive delta) and numbered `$n` as `-M extended` numbers them; `-I G`'s server-side INSERT ...
//! SELECT ... FROM generate_series at scale 1, and at a scale whose row count passes int4 (FCONST);
//! GetTableInfo's `select count(*)` and its partition query; `-i`'s DROP TABLE, CREATE TABLE (32-bit
//! and 64-bit account ids), TRUNCATE, `begin`, COPY FROM STDIN with and without FREEZE, `commit`,
//! VACUUM ANALYZE and ALTER TABLE ADD PRIMARY KEY; and the SET and SHOW libpq sends for psql
//! (PQsetClientEncoding's `set client_encoding`, PQencryptPasswordConn's `show
//! password_encryption`). The texts are the oracle's on adacachy2 (lane PG8, run r1711; lane PG9,
//! run r1801), regenerated by scripts/postgres-actions/gen_test.py.
